course: dictionary
lesson: 6411
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word musical is a good example. Read the words around it before you choose a meaning.
explain: «The school puts on a musical at Christmas.» Here musical is a noun. The clues are puts on and the school, so it means a play or film with songs and dancing. Swap in your meaning: the school puts on a play with songs and dancing. It still makes sense.
explain: «Practising a musical instrument a little every day builds skill faster than a lot once a week.» Here musical is an adjective. The clue is instrument, so musical means connected with music. An instrument is something you play to make music, so the meaning fits.
explain: Sometimes the clue is a feeling. «She has a musical voice» tells you her voice is pleasant to hear, like music. Check each meaning by putting it into the sentence, and keep the one that makes the most sense.
fact: Musical can be an adjective, which describes a thing or a person, or a noun, which names a thing.
fact: «Musical» means connected with music, as in «musical notes» and «musical instruments».
fact: «Musical» also means good at music or liking it a lot, as in «a very musical family», or pleasant to hear, like music, as in «a musical voice».
fact: A musical is a play or film where the story is told with songs and dancing, like «The Lion King» or «Matilda».
exercise: «The school puts on a musical at Christmas.» What is a musical here? | A race on the playground | A music lesson with a teacher | *A play or film with songs and dancing | A bowl of soup
exercise: «Practising a musical instrument a little every day builds skill faster than a lot once a week.» What does musical mean here? | Made of wood | *Connected with music | Very loud | Pleasant to hear
exercise: Priya says, «She has a musical voice.» What does musical suggest? | Ready for bed | Tired and sleepy | Lost in the playground | *Pleasant to hear, like music
test: «The family is very musical; they all play an instrument.» What does musical mean here? | Wet and grey | Very old | Hungry all the time | *Good at music, or liking it a lot
test: In «The school puts on a musical at Christmas», what kind of word is musical? | An adjective | A verb | *A noun | An adverb
exam: Lily says, «Musical only means music lessons.» Is she right? | Yes, it only means lessons | Yes, because lessons are the only music | No, it means a kind of bird | *No, it has more than one meaning, such as a play with songs
